---
import PortfolioDetail from '../layouts/PortfolioDetail.astro';
---

<PortfolioDetail title="Solar Offset Mobile App" heroImage="/solar-offset/mobile-app-hero.png">
  <!-- Quick Overview Section -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-12 text-gray-900">
        Quick Overview
      </h2>
      
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-6">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-semibold mb-3">What is it?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            A mobile-first app that tracks carbon credits, auto-ingests inverter data, and offers a robust help section for transparency.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-6">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-semibold mb-3">Target Audience</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Homeowners and small business owners in the province of Alberta
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-6">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-semibold mb-3">Interesting stuff I worked on</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            B2C applications, Data visualization and dashboards, Process tracking dashboards, Light mode, Mobile
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="pb-6">
          <h3 class="text-[#50A684] font-semibold mb-3">Year</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">2025</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Introduction Section -->
  <section class="py-24 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 text-gray-900">Introduction</h2>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
        <p>
          Solar Offset is a mobile-first hybrid app that assists the organic traveler (like you through a PC and API connections, provides third-party data aggregation from different carbon credit and renewable sources, and provides a visual roadmap to zero carbon offsetting. It aims to promote transparency in their carbon credit impact—and where the dollars they spend end up going.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started the project as the solo Product Designer and carried it through to development and delivery. By the end of the project, I was making product decisions as a Product Manager in a team of four developers and a designer, and was the face of the product for the stakeholder.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Problem Space Section -->
  <section class="py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-12 text-gray-900">The Problem Space</h2>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6 mb-12">
        <p>
          To understand the problem, we did by-sprint to locate Planet Offset's customers: retailers where the current segment breaks down, and according to data from Sociable. Together, we highlighted the best user journey, so the user's carbon offsetting experience is realistic through the customer's needs and how the product fits with their budget to reduce their global footprint.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Problem Space Visualization -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-md">
          <img src="/solar-offset/empathy-mapping.png" alt="Empathy mapping" class="w-full" />
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-md">
          <img src="/solar-offset/user-needs-discovery.png" alt="User needs discovery" class="w-full" />
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
        <p>
          A flow diagram sketched exactly. Solar Offset is home to hitting a windfall offering every part of their journey, a financial credit that they're awarded through carbon tracking to let them, in a realistic, user-friendly product.
        </p>
        <p>
          Using these insights, we defined our <strong>Staged Product Opportunity</strong>: take the current Solar Offset ecosystem boost plans in four throughout a beautiful, human-centered product that provides users with a realistic option for tracking carbon offsets while keeping an open-budget data flow tracking.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Design Iteration Section -->
  <section class="py-24 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-12 text-gray-900">Design Iteration 1</h2>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6 mb-12">
        <p>
          Before starting anything, we built out a Figma requirements document that captured functional and non-functional requirements, outlined user stories, and mapped the foundational user journey. This captured the foundational and non-functional requirements with the product to the optimal guidance for the user's journey.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Design Iteration Image -->
      <div class="mb-12">
        <img src="/solar-offset/design-iteration.png" alt="Design iteration wireframes" class="w-full rounded-lg shadow-md" />
      </div>
      
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6 mt-12">
        <p>
          With the requirements in place, we developed a low-fidelity prototype and brought it into testing with users following the completion. It helped us ensure users could complete the typical task, flow interactions with the product for better understand the user's journey.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Technical Analysis Section -->
  <section class="py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-12 text-gray-900">Technical Analysis + refining the prototype</h2>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6 mb-12">
        <p>
          Here, we assessed the technical feasibility and defined the product's architecture. After evaluating several architectural approaches, we settled on a single-page hybrid front-end partnered with a microservices back-end. This gave us the flexibility we needed for the reflecting, allowing the team to build efficiently while still delivering a polished product experience.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Technical Architecture Diagram -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-md">
        <img src="/solar-offset/technical-architecture-diagram.png" alt="Technical architecture" class="w-full" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final Prototype Section -->
  <section class="py-24 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-16 text-gray-900">The Final Prototype</h2>
      
      <!-- Home Screen -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center mb-24">
        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-[#E8F5F1] to-[#D8F0E8] p-12 rounded-2xl flex justify-center">
          <img src="/solar-offset/app-home-screen.png" alt="Home screen" class="w-full max-w-xs drop-shadow-xl" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">Home Screen</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            The home screen is the user gets their main on immediate trends of how they currently track their positions, and a selection action items on-the-go. This includes their portfolio, a one-year forecast, offsets, and whether their target is tracking smoothly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Submission Progress Screen -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center mb-24">
        <div class="order-2 md:order-1">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">Submission Progress Screen</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            The submission progress screen digs into the details of what's happening with a user's carbon credits, filling the transparency gap we uncovered in interviews. Each step is still ahead, as the flow is easy to follow without extra explanation. It's a simple flow to help users see where they are in the loop and understand how their credits are moving through the process.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="order-1 md:order-2 bg-gradient-to-br from-[#E8F5F1] to-[#D8F0E8] p-12 rounded-2xl flex justify-center">
          <img src="/solar-offset/app-submission-progress.png" alt="Progress screen" class="w-full max-w-xs drop-shadow-xl" />
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Inverter Connectivity Screen -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center mb-24">
        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-[#E8F5F1] to-[#D8F0E8] p-12 rounded-2xl flex justify-center">
          <img src="/solar-offset/app-connectivity.png" alt="Connectivity screen" class="w-full max-w-xs drop-shadow-xl" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">Inverter Connectivity Screen</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            The inverter connectivity screen lets users take control of the inverters tied to the user's carbon credits. Simply putting the device with inverters themselves is whether their output is tracking smoothly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Analytics -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center">
        <div class="order-2 md:order-1">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">Analytics</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            This detailed section gives users a closer look at their energy production, platform, and an estimate of their expected payout. A simple tax-year selector at the top lets you toggle through any prior year you want. While the functionality is easily accessible, making simple yearly comparisons almost trivial.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="order-1 md:order-2 bg-gradient-to-br from-[#E8F5F1] to-[#D8F0E8] p-12 rounded-2xl flex justify-center">
          <img src="/solar-offset/app-analytics.png" alt="Analytics screen" class="w-full max-w-xs drop-shadow-xl" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Curious to Connect Section -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-r from-[#4A9A7A] via-[#50A684] to-[#5BB28E] text-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-6">
        Curious to connect?
      </h2>
      <a href="/#contact" class="inline-block px-8 py-3 bg-white text-[#50A684] rounded-full hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors font-medium text-lg">
        Let's get in touch :)
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</PortfolioDetail>
